Recently, the work in [33] has shown that liver T2* and wT1 are strongly correlated and has proposed the use of the correlation results in a healthy cohort for compensating for the T2* effect on wT1. Following this, a calibration approach to estimate wT1comp is employed based only on the results of the benign-no-risk group. First, the correlation between T2* and wT1, estimated from the CIR-LL acquisition, is defined for the benign-no-risk group. Then, the slope of the correlation (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
